cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Perdrix, please cite it as below."
title: "Perdrix, an open norm for filling in DVI records"
abstract: >-
  An open norm that says how to fill in the dental part of the Interpol disaster
  victim identification (DVI) forms, ante mortem and post mortem, so that records
  entered by different experts stay comparable. One JSON file, with a reference
  Python library.
version: "0.27.3-draft"
date-released: "2026-11-22"
authors:
  - family-names: Diakonoff
    given-names: Hadrien
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://perdrix-dvi.org/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Forensic-Odontologist/perdrix"
keywords:
  - disaster victim identification
  - DVI
  - forensic odontology
  - dental records
  - Interpol
